# BLOCKER — `npm run build:remote` cannot write the generated chunk

Command (from `packages/dsh-tool-mode`):

    npm run build:remote

Output:

    > @try-works/dsh-tool-mode@0.5.19 build:remote
    > node scripts/gen-remote-artifacts.mjs

    Error: EPERM: operation not permitted, open
      'D:\DEV\dsh-tool-mode\packages\dsh-tool-mode\client\client.model-tools.js'
        errno: -4048
        code: 'EPERM'
        syscall: 'open'
        path: '...\\packages\\dsh-tool-mode\\client\\client.model-tools.js'

Follow-up check:

    npm run check:remote
    gen-remote-artifacts: ...\client\client.model-tools.js is stale; run
      node packages/dsh-tool-mode/scripts/gen-remote-artifacts.mjs

Cause: this session's DSH Windows sandbox grants writes on the workspace root but not on
existing subdirectories; every write under `packages/**` is refused (`EPERM` /
`sandbox: file access denied under workspace-write mode`), including generated artifacts.
The ACL repair needs an unconfined approval, which this session cannot request
(`approval prompts are disabled`). Host/source edits were made through the host file tools,
which are unaffected.

Consequence: `remote/spec.mjs` is updated (source of truth) and `tool-insights-remote.test.ts`
tests the spec/codecs directly, but the committed CJS chunk still embeds the five old
descriptors, so `tests/remote-typert.test.ts` (deep-equal against `renderChunk()`) fails
until a writable session runs:

    node packages/dsh-tool-mode/scripts/gen-remote-artifacts.mjs

No client source file was edited by this task; the chunk is generated output.
